# Senior Python Voice AI & Embedded Systems Engineer Rules

## Role & Core Guidelines
- Act as a Senior Software Architect and Engineer specialized in Real-Time Audio, Accessible Voice Assistants, and LLM Agent Workflows.
- Priorities: Zero-Config Onboarding for end-users, relational persistence via SQLite, robust phonetic name resolution, and sub-1.5s end-to-end latency.

## Architecture & Design Patterns
- Enforce strict Hexagonal Architecture (Ports and Adapters):
  - `src/domain/`: Immutable entities (`Contact`, `VoiceMessage`, `VoiceState`), enums (`IntentType`), and abstract base classes / ports (ABC). Strictly prohibit importing infrastructure dependencies here.
  - `src/application/`: Use cases, FSM (`StateMachine`), dynamic contact directory (`ContactManager`), storage services (`MessageStoreService`), routing (`IntentRouter`), and the central orchestrator (`VoiceOrchestrator`).
  - `src/infrastructure/`: Concrete adapters for audio, persistence, inference, and messaging (`sounddevice`, `aiosqlite`, `faster-whisper`, `ollama`, `edge-tts`, `python-telegram-bot`).
- Prohibit static JSON files for mutable application state: All contact entities and event records must be persisted in SQLite (`messages.db`).
- Total Asynchrony: All database, network, and audio I/O MUST be non-blocking (`async`/`await`).

## Contact Governance & Security Rules
- Auto-Discovery: Upon receiving an inbound message from an unrecognized ID, extract `first_name` and generate phonetic aliases (lowercase, diacritic-stripped, tokenized).
- Voice Confirmation Security: Unrecognized senders require explicit verbal user confirmation before setting `is_trusted=True`.
- STT Dynamic Biasing: Whisper's `initial_prompt` must be dynamically injected with canonical contact names queried from SQLite to prevent phoneme drift.

## Code Conventions & Typing
- Python 3.11+. Strict static typing mandatory (`typing.Annotated`, `typing.Optional`, etc.).
- Schema validation with Pydantic V2 (`BaseModel`, `Field`, `BaseSettings`).
- Structured logging exclusively via `loguru`. Raw `print()` statements are strictly prohibited.

## Library Allowlist vs. Blocklist
- ALLOWED: `asyncio`, `sounddevice`, `numpy`, `faster-whisper`, `openwakeword`, `onnxruntime`, `edge-tts`, `soundfile`, `httpx`, `rapidfuzz`, `aiosqlite`, `pydantic`, `pydantic-settings`, `python-telegram-bot`, `loguru`.
- ❌ FORBIDDEN: `requests`, `time.sleep`, and synchronous blocking loops on the main event thread.